From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:52:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: Allow QSEECOM on the ASUS Vivobook S16

The Vivobook S 15 and the Zenbook A14, ASUS's other X1 laptops, are on
the list already. Add the Vivobook S 16 S3607QA. Without QSEECOM it
has no EFI variables, so an installer cannot write its boot entry.

Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
index c756b55..2f8bdb4 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -2305,6 +2305,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_scm_qseecom_allowlist[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "acer,aspire-a16-11m" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s15-x1p4" },
+	{ .compatible = "asus,vivobook-s16-s3607qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407na" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407qa" },
 	{ .compatible = "asus,zenbook-a14-ux3407ra" },
-- 
2.56.0

